  "Question": "If \\(f(n)=\\dfrac13n(n+1)(n+2),\\) then \\(f(r)-f(r-1)\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(r(r+1)\\)",
    "B": "\\((r+1)(r+2)\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac13r(r+1)\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac13(r+1)(r+2)\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac13r(r+1)(r+2)\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Substituting \\(r-1\\) into the formula gives\n\\[\nf(r-1)=\\frac13(r-1)r(r+1).\n\\]\nThe expressions for \\(f(r)\\) and \\(f(r-1)\\) share the factors \\(r\\) and \\(r+1\\). Factoring them out avoids expanding the cubic products:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(r)-f(r-1)\n&=\\frac{r(r+1)}3\\bigl[(r+2)-(r-1)\\bigr]\\\\\n&=\\frac{r(r+1)}3\\cdot3\\\\\n&=r(r+1).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThus the answer is \\(r(r+1)\\), choice A.",
